x86/microcode/AMD: Handle the case of no BIOS microcode

jira KERNEL-814
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.115.1.el8_10
commit-author Borislav Petkov (AMD) <bp@alien8.de>
commit fcf8239ad6a5de54fa7ce18e464c6b5951b982cb
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.115.1.el8_10/fcf8239a.failed

Machines can be shipped without any microcode in the BIOS. Which means,
the microcode patch revision is 0.

Handle that gracefully.

Fixes: 94838d230a6c ("x86/microcode/AMD: Use the family,model,stepping encoded in the patch ID")
	Reported-by: Vítek Vávra <vit.vavra.kh@gmail.com>
	Signed-off-by: Borislav Petkov (AMD) <bp@alien8.de>
	Cc: <stable@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit fcf8239ad6a5de54fa7ce18e464c6b5951b982cb)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

